{"uid":"d1f312957c98a7ee","name":"test_repointing_alone_is_bounded_as_a_stagnation_escape","fullName":"tests.test_worker_split_proposal#test_repointing_alone_is_bounded_as_a_stagnation_escape","historyId":"b9772bca204d0f0ce0f54628429f5c08","time":{"start":1791930737946,"stop":1791930738312,"duration":366},"description":"The counterpart of `test_a_worker_that_only_ever_proposes_splits_\n    still_fails_the_approach` above, for the second side channel, and the\n    node the whole fold into this module is justified by: a worker whose\n    every reply carries ONLY a `proposed_task_updates` re-point still reaches\n    the stagnation outcome.\n\n    It is owed precisely because this channel's answer is the opposite of the\n    split channel's. A re-point edits an EXISTING row, so\n    `state.tasks_doc_excluding_new_entries` cannot filter it out of the\n    pass's progress diff and an ACCEPTED re-point does reset the guard -- the\n    run below needs more than three worker iterations for exactly that\n    reason, where a worker that only proposed splits paused at three. What\n    bounds it is `worker_repoint_budget_per_approach` (left at its DEFAULT\n    here, so the pin is on the shipped number): four doomed dependents are\n    on offer, the fourth re-point is refused whole on budget, and from there\n    the worker buys no progress at all and the approach stagnates and pauses\n    anyway. Every guard in `lint_worker_task_updates` is legal in this\n    script, so what is measured is the budget alone.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The counterpart of <code>test_a_worker_that_only_ever_proposes_splits_ still_fails_the_approach</code> above, for the second side channel, and the<br />\nnode the whole fold into this module is justified by: a worker whose<br />\nevery reply carries ONLY a <code>proposed_task_updates</code> re-point still reaches<br />\nthe stagnation outcome.</p>\n<pre><code>It is owed precisely because this channel's answer is the opposite of the\nsplit channel's. A re-point edits an EXISTING row, so\n`state.tasks_doc_excluding_new_entries` cannot filter it out of the\npass's progress diff and an ACCEPTED re-point does reset the guard -- the\nrun below needs more than three worker iterations for exactly that\nreason, where a worker that only proposed splits paused at three. What\nbounds it is `worker_repoint_budget_per_approach` (left at its DEFAULT\nhere, so the pin is on the shipped number): four doomed dependents are\non offer, the fourth re-point is refused whole on budget, and from there\nthe worker buys no progress at all and the approach stagnates and pauses\nanyway. Every guard in `lint_worker_task_updates` is legal in this\nscript, so what is measured is the budget alone.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791930737918,"stop":1791930737918,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791930737918,"stop":1791930737929,"duration":11},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791930737930,"stop":1791930737930,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791930737931,"stop":1791930737939,"duration":8},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_esc